window.docContents[108].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Deploying-a-domain-model___-the-deployment-template--The-template":{"contents":"The rows below are generated from PropertyKindCalculus.Rubrics.deploymentTemplate. The\nauthor's part column is the one to read while building a document; the sections that\nfollow argue why each group asks for what it asks. Conformance is declared exactly as for\nthe model template: declaration sites through the @[rubric …] attribute, section sites\nthrough the document's own tags, and a status computed from the two against each rubric's\nevidence kind.\n\n* * Requires* The rubric* The author's part* What is deployed* * * * D1* exposition* What is deployed, and which model boundary each deployed unit realizes* List the deployed units, and name for each the model boundary it realizes* D2* exposition* The document states what deploying the model adds, and cites the model document for what the module is* State what deploying the model adds, and cite the model document for what the module is* The contracts* * * * D3* checked* The data contract is declared, compiled in, and validated against a producer's own claims before any payload is decoded* Declare the payload interface, compile it into the executable, and validate it against the producer's own claims before any payload is decoded* D4* checked* The platform contract is kind-typed and held to the registration payload, with the discharge relation decided by the kernel* Kind-type the argument plane the scheduler passes, hold it to the registration payload, and let the kernel decide the discharge relation between the two* D5* generated* One deployment card per deployed unit, each panel read off a declared object rather than written beside it* Generate one deployment card per deployed unit, each panel read off a declared object rather than written beside it* Sizing and knobs* * * * D6* measured* The run is sized from measured records, not from constants typed by hand* Size the run from measured records, and name the records each size came from* D7* measured* Operating points come from a sweep whose own turnover or plateau names them, reported with the dispersion any threshold has to beat* Sweep the parameter, let the machine's own turnover or plateau name the operating point, and report the dispersion any threshold has to beat* D8* exposition* Every environment knob a job may set is enumerated with what it decides* Enumerate every environment knob a job may set, with what each one decides* The platform* * * * D9* exposition* The image facts are stated: what ships per unit, the toolchain and architecture spectrum it was built for, and the ABI floor it runs against* State what ships per unit, the toolchain and architecture spectrum it was built for, and the ABI floor it runs against* D10* exposition* Registration and version derivation are mechanized, so a deployed version is derived from the artifact rather than asserted beside it* Derive the deployed version from the artifact and mechanize registration, so neither is asserted beside what actually shipped* D11* exposition* Backend interchange is stated: what the same source does on each target, and what changes when the target changes* State what the same source does on each target, and what changes when the target does* Acceptance* * * * D12* checked* Acceptance is a gate against the specification the model document proves — run as proof-by-execution, not asserted* Run acceptance as a gate against the specification the model document proves — proof by execution, not an assertion that the two agree* D13* measured* Performance claims are a paired A/B in the deployed executable, never a microbenchmark quoted as a prediction* Make every performance claim a paired A/B in the deployed executable, never a microbenchmark quoted as a prediction* D14* exposition* Each green signal names which of the changed lines it actually compiled or ran, so a passing pipeline is not quoted as evidence for a path it never touched* Say, for each green signal quoted as evidence, which of the changed lines it actually compiled or ran* Reproducibility and limits* * * * D15* exposition* Failure, checkpoint and resume semantics are stated: what a partially completed job leaves behind, and what resuming it does* State what a partially completed job leaves behind, and what resuming it does with that* D16* generated* A reproducibility manifest carries the pins and digests of what actually ran, generated from the artifacts rather than transcribed* Generate the reproducibility manifest from the artifacts — the pins and digests of what actually ran, not of what was intended* D17* exposition* What is trusted is stated plainly: the boundaries the verification does not cross, and what a consumer is therefore taking on faith* Name the boundaries this deployment's verification does not cross, and what a consumer is therefore taking on faith\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Deploying a domain model: the deployment template","header":"33.1. The template","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Deploying-a-domain-model___-the-deployment-template--The-template"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--The-Proved-Spine--Metrological-units-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-18___-___13___3___3_RPAR_":{"contents":"\n\nA metrological unit (§18.12) carries the kind it\nreferences and a terminological symbol (the unit id, e.g. \"m\", \"kg\"). A kind\nbears a unit (BearsUnit, §13.3.3) iff its scale is at least differential, and a\nunit is well-formed iff its kind bears one; measure u n builds the\nproperty value \"n × symbol\".\n\nA structure with DecidableEq. BearsUnit is scale.AllowsDifference,\nWellFormed is kind.BearsUnit, and measure fills the value's numeral and\nreference fields from n and the unit's symbol.\n\nCommensurability is an equivalence. Two units are\ncommensurable iff they reference the same kind (§9.13.4); the relation is\nreflexive, symmetric, and transitive. A metre and a centimetre are commensurable;\na metre and a kilogram are not — incommensurability across kinds is a fact of the\ntypes, not a runtime check. Transitivity is exactly the law a description logic\ncannot state.\n\nCommensurability unfolds to equality of the kind field, so reflexivity,\nsymmetry, and transitivity are those of Eq.\n\nOnly a unitary kind bears a unit. A nominal kind has no magnitude, and — the\ndistinctive §9.13.4 fact — an ordinal kind, though rankable, has no\nreference-times-number magnitude either, so neither bears a metrological unit\n(not_wellFormed_of_nominal, not_wellFormed_of_ordinal). Conversely a rational\nkind does (rational_bears_unit), and bearing a unit implies being a\nkind-of-quantity (bearsUnit_isQuantity). This gate is invisible to a\ndimension-and-scale-only view that treats every magnitude alike. Uses the metrological unit.\n\nBearsUnit is scale.AllowsDifference, which is False at nominal and ordinal;\nsubstitute the scale from IsNominal/IsOrdinal and the goal is ¬ False. The\nrational case and bearsUnit_isQuantity are the same four-way case split on the\nscale.\n\nThe number-and-reference form is a faithful round-trip (§13.3.3). Measuring a\nquantity in a unit yields a numeral, and re-applying the unit to that numeral\nrecovers the value:\n\nSo quantity / unit = number and number × unit = quantity invert one another —\nthe §13.3.3 \"reference quantity multiplied by a number\", checked as a law. Measuring\nin a well-formed unit moreover yields a quantity value\n(measure_isQuantityValue), and values measured in commensurable units are comparable. Builds on the metrological unit.\n\nmeasure_numeral is rfl. For the converse, destructure \"measured in u\" into the\nkind- and reference-equalities, unfold measure, and rewrite the unit's kind and\nsymbol back to the value's fields; structure eta closes the goal.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009The Proved Spine","header":"5.6. Metrological units (Dybkær Ch. 18, §13.3.3)","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--The-Proved-Spine--Metrological-units-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-18___-___13___3___3_RPAR_"}});